#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147162 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147482 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a0e1c05a-7c23-59f5-a549-ec9a8d0415e6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage"}] :question/id #uuid "034e763d-a3e1-52e8-90a7-9fac9ce11083" :question/math-academy-id "e-13108" :question/problem "What is $4 \\%$ of $35$?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}= \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $35$, and the percentage is $4 \\%$.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n4 \\% = 4 \\div 100 = 0.04\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 4% \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= 0.04 \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= 1.4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4 \\%$ of $35$ is $1.4$.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n4 \\% = \\dfrac{4}{100}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 4% \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{100} \\cdot 35 \\\\\n&= \\frac{140}{100} \\\\\n&= 1.4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4 \\%$ of $35$ is $1.4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147163 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147483 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20feb2c2-bcec-5730-be40-da2f8e44be59" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage Greater Than 100%"}] :question/id #uuid "a5fc07bc-6168-5525-acfb-a36ee021773d" :question/math-academy-id "e-13109" :question/problem "What is $140 \\%$ of $30$?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}= \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $30$, and the percentage is $140\\%$.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140 \\% = 140 \\div 100 = 1.4\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 140% \\cdot 30 \\\\\n&= 1.4 \\cdot 30 \\\\\n&= 42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140 \\%$ of $30$ is $42$.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n140 \\% = \\dfrac{140}{100} = \\dfrac{140 \\div 20}{100\\div 20} = \\dfrac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 140% \\cdot 30 \\\\\n&= \\frac{7}{5} \\cdot 30 \\\\\n&= 7 \\cdot \\frac{30}{5} \\\\\n&= 7 \\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140 \\%$ of $30$ is $42$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147164 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147484 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0025f8a6-40fc-544b-abc7-e9c283da8f33" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage"}] :question/id #uuid "8dde0f33-28c8-569b-a1f8-9390d8dafc35" :question/math-academy-id "e-13110" :question/problem "What is $3.6 \\%$ of $25$?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}= \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $25$, and the percentage is $3.6 \\%$.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n3.6 \\% = 3.6 \\div 100 = 0.036\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 3.6% \\cdot 25 \\\\\n&= 0.036 \\cdot 25 \\\\\n&= 0.9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3.6 \\%$ of $25$ is $0.9$.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n3.6 \\% = \\dfrac{3.6}{100} = \\dfrac{3.6 \\times 10}{100 \\times 10} = \\dfrac{36}{1,000}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\npart &= percentage \\cdot whole \\\\\n&= 3.6% \\cdot 25 \\\\\n&= \\frac{36}{1, 000} \\cdot 25 \\\\\n&= \\frac{900}{1, 000} \\\\\n&= 0.9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3.6 \\%$ of $25$ is $0.9$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147483 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "20feb2c2-bcec-5730-be40-da2f8e44be59" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Percentage Greater Than 100%"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afbac020-f132-5e21-a592-ba884a925e15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145095} {:answer/id #uuid "d95d4dde-2d2e-55f4-a211-e1e0ec70664b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145096} {:answer/id #uuid "de66d9e6-7a8b-5ad9-a2ad-8e52d88220f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145097} {:answer/id #uuid "13c043e3-9d6b-5110-b016-6b7b2ebf3cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145098} {:answer/id #uuid "789c7308-d1a5-5b0c-9c15-595b95d781b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145099}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c37a885d-7e2b-5e81-bc52-ff2753974527" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186145094}] :question/id #uuid "9bc7c273-0dfe-58b5-98ac-f3b5aaeadbfa" :question/math-academy-id "q-61533" :question/problem "What is $120%$ of $25$?"}]}
